IMPORT prelude

-- Wyoming's refund of state taxes for residents 65 or over or totally disabled, W.S. 39-11-109(c) -- Wyoming has no income tax
-- (W.S. 39-7-101, 39-12-101; encoded in ../../../wyoming-statutes-title-39-taxation-and-revenue-chapters-7-and-12-income-tax/
-- encodings/baseline-2026-10/), so this income-tested refund "of taxes paid under the sales and use taxes, property tax relief
-- and utility or energy cost relief" (39-11-109(c)(v)) is the personal tax provision an individual meets. Encoded: who is a
-- "resident" and "totally disabled" (39-11-109(c)(i)(D), (F)), who qualifies (c)(ii), the asset test and its exemptions
-- (c)(vii), the amount and its reductions (c)(ii), (viii), the application deadline and the date the refund must be mailed
-- (c)(iii), (iv).
--
-- SEAT: the Wyoming resident aged 65 or over, or totally disabled, who applies for the refund ("Do I qualify? How much? By when
-- must I apply, and when will it come?").
--
-- Edition: the Legislative Service Office's title 39 PDF (created 2026-10-14), downloaded 2026-10-19, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/wy-stat-39-ch11.txt (unofficial).
--
-- INPUTS. The asset ceiling of $25,000 per adult is "adjusted annually by the state average Wyoming cost-of-living index"
-- (c)(vii): the figure for the year is an input whose @desc names the printed amount. The appropriation fraction of (c)(viii)(A)
-- is set each fiscal year by the department of health from the appropriation and total claims: an input (1 if the appropriation
-- covers every claim).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Rules of the department of health under (c)(vi) (not deposited); the remaining provisions of W.S. 39-11-109
-- (subsections (a), (b), (d)) and the rest of chapter 11 (administration of taxes generally).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wyoming refund for the elderly and disabled -- W.S. 39-11-109(c)`

§§ `The parties and the actions`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the department of health`

DECLARE `Action` IS ONE OF
    `apply under oath with a copy of last year's federal return or a statement that none was required`
    `mail the refund warrant with its letter of transmittal`

§§ `W.S. 39-11-109(c)(i)-(ii) -- who qualifies`

-- (c)(i)(D): "'Resident' means a person who has been a resident of Wyoming and domiciled within Wyoming for a period of not less
-- than one (1) year and who has not claimed residency elsewhere for any purpose for the one (1) year period immediately
-- preceding the date of application".
GIVEN `months resident and domiciled in Wyoming` IS A NUMBER
      `claimed residency elsewhere in the last year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a resident for the refund` IF
    `months resident and domiciled in Wyoming` AT LEAST 12 AND NOT (`claimed residency elsewhere in the last year`)

-- (c)(i)(F): "'Totally disabled' means a person eighteen (18) years of age or older whose physical or mental condition permanently
-- prevents the person from performing any substantial gainful employment during the one (1) year period immediately preceding
-- the date of application".
-- (c)(ii): "Wyoming residents meeting asset eligibility requirements ... who are sixty-five (65) years of age and older or who are
-- eighteen (18) years of age and older and are totally disabled during the one (1) year period ... and are not residents of any
-- state funded institution, are qualified".
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `a condition has permanently prevented any substantial gainful employment for the past year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is aged or totally disabled` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 65 OR (`age` AT LEAST 18 AND `a condition has permanently prevented any substantial gainful employment for the past year`)

-- (c)(vii): "No applicant is entitled to a refund ... unless the person has total household assets ... not to exceed twenty-five
-- thousand dollars ($25,000.00) per adult member of the household as adjusted annually". Exempt: "(A) The structure and lands
-- occupied as the applicant's primary residence; (B) Household furnishings and personal belongings; (C) One (1) personal motor
-- vehicle per adult in the household; (D) Assets held under a bona fide pension plan or individual retirement account (IRA);
-- (E) The cash value of any life insurance policies held." (The person states assets other than those.)
GIVEN `household assets other than the exempt kinds` IS A NUMBER
      `adults in the household` IS A NUMBER
      `asset ceiling per adult for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the asset test` IF
    `household assets other than the exempt kinds` AT MOST (`adults in the household` TIMES `asset ceiling per adult for the year`)

§§ `W.S. 39-11-109(c)(ii), (viii) -- the amount`

-- (c)(ii): "a qualified single person whose actual income is less than seventeen thousand five hundred dollars ($17,500.00) shall
-- receive eight hundred dollars ($800.00) reduced by the percentage that his actual income exceeds ten thousand dollars
-- ($10,000.00) per year and qualified married persons, at least one (1) of whom is at least sixty-five (65) years of age or
-- totally disabled, whose actual income is less than twenty-eight thousand five hundred dollars ($28,500.00) shall receive nine
-- hundred dollars ($900.00) reduced by the percentage that their actual income exceeds sixteen thousand dollars ($16,000.00)".
-- "The percentage that income exceeds $10,000" is read as (income - 10,000) / 10,000 (NOTES.md finding 2). "Until remarriage a
-- person sixty (60) years or older once qualified through marriage remains eligible individually for single person benefits".
GIVEN `married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `actual income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount before reductions` `married` `actual income` MEANS
    IF `actual income` AT LEAST `limit`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `full` TIMES (1 MINUS `percentage over`)
    WHERE
        `full`            MEANS IF `married` THEN 900 ELSE 800
        `limit`           MEANS IF `married` THEN 28500 ELSE 17500
        `base`            MEANS IF `married` THEN 16000 ELSE 10000
        `percentage over` MEANS (max 0 (`actual income` MINUS `base`)) DIVIDED BY `base`

-- (c)(viii): "Any refund ... shall be reduced by the dollar amount received by the applicant for the preceding calendar year from
-- any exemption under W.S. 39-13-105, any homeowner's tax credit under W.S. 39-13-109(d)(i) or any tax refund under W.S.
-- 39-13-109(c)(v)", and (A) multiplied by the appropriation fraction, "In no event shall the refund be greater than the amounts
-- specified in paragraph (ii)". The order (reduction, then fraction) follows the paragraph's order.
GIVEN `amount before reductions` IS A NUMBER
      `property tax relief received for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `appropriation fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund` `amount before reductions` `property tax relief received for the preceding year` `appropriation fraction` MEANS
    (max 0 (`amount before reductions` MINUS `property tax relief received for the preceding year`)) TIMES (min 1 `appropriation fraction`)

§§ `W.S. 39-11-109(c)(iii)-(iv) -- applying, and the warrant`

-- (c)(iii): "Qualified residents shall apply ... on or before the last working day in August of each year ... under oath ... and
-- shall be accompanied by a copy of the applicant's federal income tax return for the previous calendar year or a statement under
-- oath that the applicant was not required to file a return". Applying is the person's choice: not applying is no breach, but
-- the refund is then lost for the year. Written with DO ... LEST FULFILLED, the department's duty following under HENCE.
-- (c)(iv): "Warrants for tax refunds shall be mailed by the department to qualified recipients by December 20 following the
-- application date". Counted in days: the days from today to the last working day in August, then from then to December 20.
GIVEN `days to the last working day in August` IS A NUMBER
      `days from then to December 20` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my application for the refund` `days to the last working day in August` `days from then to December 20` MEANS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    DO     `apply under oath with a copy of last year's federal return or a statement that none was required`
    WITHIN `days to the last working day in August`
    HENCE  `the warrant I must be sent` `days from then to December 20`
    LEST   FULFILLED

GIVEN `days to December 20` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`the warrant I must be sent` `days to December 20` MEANS
    PARTY  `the department of health`
    MUST   `mail the refund warrant with its letter of transmittal`
    WITHIN `days to December 20`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the department of health` BECAUSE "refund warrant not mailed by December 20 (W.S. 39-11-109(c)(iv))"

§ `Questions for the applicant`

§§ `Do I qualify?`

@export Do I qualify for Wyoming's refund of state taxes for people 65 or over or totally disabled (W.S. 39-11-109(c)(i), (ii), (vii))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `a condition has kept me from any substantial gainful work for the past year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physical or mental condition has permanently prevented you from any substantial gainful employment during the year before you apply
      `months I have lived in and been domiciled in Wyoming` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months you have been a Wyoming resident and domiciled in Wyoming, up to the date of application
      `I claimed residency elsewhere in the last year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claimed residency in another place for any purpose during the year before you apply
      `I live in a state-funded institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a resident of a state-funded institution
      `our household assets other than the exempt kinds` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's total assets, in US dollars, leaving out your home and its land, furnishings and personal belongings, one car per adult, pension and IRA assets, and the cash value of life insurance
      `adults in our household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adults live in your household
      `the asset ceiling per adult for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The asset ceiling per adult for the year as adjusted by the Wyoming cost-of-living index; the statute prints 25000
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I qualify for the elderly and disabled refund` IF
        `is aged or totally disabled` `my age` `a condition has kept me from any substantial gainful work for the past year`
    AND `is a resident for the refund` `months I have lived in and been domiciled in Wyoming` `I claimed residency elsewhere in the last year`
    AND (NOT (`I live in a state-funded institution`))
    AND `meets the asset test` `our household assets other than the exempt kinds` `adults in our household` `the asset ceiling per adult for the year`

§§ `How much will I get?`

@export How much is my Wyoming refund for the elderly and disabled (W.S. 39-11-109(c)(ii), (viii)), if I qualify?
GIVEN `I am married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply as a married person (at least one spouse 65 or over or totally disabled); a widow or widower aged 60 or over who first qualified through marriage applies as single until remarriage
      `our actual income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your actual income for the year (with your spouse's, if married), in US dollars, including wages, self-employment, rents, interest, dividends, pensions, Social Security, public assistance, unemployment and veterans' and disability benefits
      `property tax relief we got for last year` IS A NUMBER @desc What you received for the preceding calendar year from the veterans' property tax exemption (W.S. 39-13-105), the homeowner's tax credit (39-13-109(d)(i)) or the property tax refund (39-13-109(c)(v)), in US dollars; 0 if none
      `the appropriation fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction the department of health applies when the appropriation does not cover all refunds (1 if it does)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my elderly and disabled refund` `I am married` `our actual income` `property tax relief we got for last year` `the appropriation fraction` MEANS
    `the refund` (`the amount before reductions` `I am married` `our actual income`) `property tax relief we got for last year` `the appropriation fraction`
